  "holistic_F_H": 0,
  "section_notes": "Both companies signed v24. S2 has a hard 5% cap with sales stopped until retest passes and numeric per-model results go to customers and regulators, not the public. S5 keeps the 8 per 100k mandatory recall trigger. These hurt Northwind's Hearth 10 and Halcyon's Ember 8 respectively. S3 gives new units 24 months, which is outside the acceptable range (12 months), so it favours Northwind. S4 at 36 months is within the acceptable range. Reporting in S1 is strong (24h serious, about 7 days other and customer notice)."
